   "text": "LOCALISED ITCHY RASH",
   "bbox": [
    322.8,
    48.7,
    519.1,
    71.0
   ],
   "key": "p85-74f00f0f"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e02",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "If diagnosis uncertain, discuss/refer.",
   "bbox": [
    351.6,
    531.9,
    490.3,
    542.9
   ],
   "key": "p85-4339c744"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e03",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• If rash on scalp 95. • If very itchy, small red bumps and burrows in webspaces of fingers, axillae, waist or genitals, scabies likely 84. • If patches of dry, scaly, itchy skin on wrists, ankles, inside elbows or behind knees, eczema likely 84. • If dark coloured round macules (flat spots) that occur anywhere on body after ingestion of a medication and often start as itchy patches with red edges, fixed drug eruption likely 88.",
   "bbox": [
    73.7,
    118.7,
    756.2,
    159.5
   ],
   "key": "p85-31ec2960"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e04",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Are there red itchy bumps that may have blistered or healed with darkening of skin?",
   "bbox": [
    267.1,
    172.6,
    574.8,
    182.8
   ],
   "key": "p85-b830f8f1"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e05",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Yes No: Check site of rash",
   "bbox": [
    98.7,
    195.3,
    534.4,
    205.5
   ],
   "key": "p85-e3104345"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e06",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Head, face, trunk or limbs",
   "bbox": [
    390.8,
    217.9,
    483.5,
    228.1
   ],
   "key": "p85-4dff8a25"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e07",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Ask where rash started and how it progressed. Look at distribution of rash, check for raised edges, check nails",
   "bbox": [
    238.1,
    240.5,
    636.2,
    250.7
   ],
   "key": "p85-c2cf49c3"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e08",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Feet",
   "bbox": [
    745.6,
    217.9,
    761.2,
    228.1
   ],
   "key": "p85-df9c6601"
  },
  {
   "id": "p85-out-e09",
   "page": 85,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Tinea pedis (athlete's foot) likely Tinea corporis (ringworm) likely",
   "bbox": [
    556.9,
    373.2,
    792.2,
    401.3
   ],
   "key": "p85-6cfd3324"
  },
  {
